            <ArticleTitle>Eosinophilic granulomatosis with polyangiitis and mononeuritis multiplex responded to induction cyclophosphamide.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr-2016-218252</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2016-218252</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of 28-year-old Malay woman who initially presented with multiple joints pain with underlying poorly controlled asthma since her childhood. She was treated as seronegative arthritis. However, the involvement of joints, asthma and high-eosinophil counts raised suspicion of Churg-Strauss syndrome. This disease is undoubtedly rare in Malaysians or even in Asian populations. After appropriate therapy was delivered for the correct diagnosis her clinical condition improved. She is currently receiving maintenance treatment.</AbstractText>
